    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green with all tests passing. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Owner deletion is now a soft-delete\n\n**What changed**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`, primitive `boolean` defaulting to `false`) with `isDeleted()` / `setDeleted()`. A new owner is `false` by default.\n\n2. **API schema** (`resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` schema. The generated `OwnerDto` picks it up and MapStruct maps it by name, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `deleted`.\n\n3. **DB schema** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `deleted` column (`NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE`) to the `owners` table, so existing seed rows read back as `false`.\n\n4. **Controller** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n   - `deleteOwner` now sets `deleted = true` and saves (retaining the row), still returning `204` (2xx), instead of removing the record.\n   - The create endpoint's two blocking checks \u2014 the hard **identity-key** duplicate loop and the **household** duplicate check (`householdMembers`) \u2014 now skip owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**Verification** \u2014 both new acceptance tests pass (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`: delete flags `deleted` true while GET still returns the owner; `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`: recreating a deep copy of a soft-deleted owner is allowed): `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: I left the soft-deleted owner still visible to `GET`/`listOwners` and still counted by the *non-blocking* derivations (`namesakeCount`, `cityOwnerCount`, `customerCode` collision, `possibleDuplicateOf`). The spec only required deleted owners to be readable-with-`deleted=true` and ignored by the **duplicate/identity** checks, so I scoped the exclusion to exactly those checks. If you'd also want deleted owners hidden from list results or excluded from those quota/derivation counts, that's a straightforward follow-up.",
